abstract: >-
  IxD Lab is an open educational resource for learning interaction design by
  making, testing, and reflecting. Fifteen browser-based labs in three modules
  (Discover, Design, Evaluate) cover research methods, interviews, personas,
  journey mapping, information architecture, wireframing, interaction patterns,
  UX writing, laws of UX, heuristic evaluation, usability testing and metrics,
  accessibility, behaviour analytics, A/B testing, and ethics. Each lab has
  explanations, a quiz, and optional AI feedback and tutoring. The software is released under the MIT License and the
  educational content under CC BY 4.0.
